The SP (Soul Power) System

This is the core mechanic you requested:

How it works:
1. Soul Power is a stockpiled resource generated by:
   - Special terrains (Ley Lines, Crystal Caverns, Haunted Grounds, Sacred Groves, Aetheric Rifts)
   - Buildings (Mana Siphon, Soul Forge, Ley Line Tap, etc.)
   - Improvements (Ley Line Channel, Soul Node)
   - Certain units (Arcane Apprentice, Elementalist, Necromancer, Summoner, etc.)
   - Racial abilities (e.g., High Elves get +2 SP from Forests)

2. Soul Conduit I through X are national wonders that consume SP and provide stacking percentage bonuses:
   - Conduit I: +5% unit strength, +5% city strength (costs 50 SP)
   - Conduit II: +10% unit strength, +10% city strength (costs 100 SP)
   - Conduit III: +15% / +15% (costs 200 SP)
   - ...up to Conduit X: +50% unit strength, +50% city strength (costs 2000 SP)

3. Each Conduit tier requires the previous one plus a minimum accumulated SP amount, creating a natural progression system where the more SP you accumulate, the stronger your entire civilization becomes.

